of wall). Add the fifo to the existing `cleanup` trap. (Do NOT point fd 3 at the console fifo itself — reading it would steal the runner's output from `tee`.)\n\nAlternatively `sleep 1` would also work but forks the child you deliberately avoided, so the fifo timer is the closer match to the stated constraint. The ≤1 s drain loop at `:195` is bounded and can keep the `/dev/zero` form or take the same fix."
